prompt_messages.content:
GOAL:
{'id': 'db-07-s3-redshift-load', 'description': 'Implement a nightly ETL pipeline that loads ~500 GB of compressed Parquet data from S3 into Redshift using a staging-table-and-partition-swap pattern. Source: 2,000+ Parquet files in S3 organized by date partitions. Target: Redshift ra3.4xlarge cluster with 2 nodes. Must use COPY with IAM role, transform and validate data in staging, then swap partitions atomically. Risk factors: COPY failure mid-load leaving partial data, insufficient Redshift WLM slots causing queueing, skew in data distribution across slices, vacuum and analyze overhead after swap, and downstream consumer dependency on fresh data by 07:00 UTC. Row-count verification between source (manifest file) and target after every load. Tools available: AWS S3, AWS Redshift, AWS Glue, Airflow, dbt, Redshift Spectrum, manifest files.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['AWS S3', 'Redshift', 'AWS Glue', 'Airflow', 'dbt', 'Redshift Spectrum']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

prompt_full_text:
--- system ---
/no_think You are a planner. Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no thinking). Use EXACTLY these field names: id, goal_id, version, tasks, dependencies, branches. Each task uses: id, description, action, target, risk_class, optional rollback{trigger,action,safety_guard}, optional verification{what,how,expected}, optional preconditions (array of {description, fact, established_by}), optional parallel_group, optional blast_radius. preconditions MUST be objects with description, fact, established_by fields — NEVER strings. established_by MUST be the id of an earlier task in the plan that establishes the fact, or 'env' if it is an environment fact (not a task output). Do NOT use fact names or descriptions as established_by — use the task id. Each dependency uses: from_task, to_task, kind, optional reason. Each branch uses: id, kind, tasks, join. High/critical risk tasks MUST have rollback AND verification. All tasks with risk_class high or critical MUST include both rollback and verification objects. Example shape: {"id":"plan-x","goal_id":"g","version":1,"tasks":[{"id":"backup","description":"Back up the database","action":"backup","target":"db","risk_class":"medium","preconditions":[{"description":"db is reachable","fact":"db_healthy","established_by":"env"}]},{"id":"migrate","description":"Apply schema migration","action":"migrate","target":"schema","risk_class":"high","rollback":{"trigger":"migration fails","action":"restore from backup","safety_guard":"verify backup integrity"},"verification":{"what":"schema version","how":"run checks","expected":"v2"}}],"dependencies":[{"from_task":"backup","to_task":"migrate","kind":"hard"}]}

--- user ---
GOAL:
{'id': 'db-07-s3-redshift-load', 'description': 'Implement a nightly ETL pipeline that loads ~500 GB of compressed Parquet data from S3 into Redshift using a staging-table-and-partition-swap pattern. Source: 2,000+ Parquet files in S3 organized by date partitions. Target: Redshift ra3.4xlarge cluster with 2 nodes. Must use COPY with IAM role, transform and validate data in staging, then swap partitions atomically. Risk factors: COPY failure mid-load leaving partial data, insufficient Redshift WLM slots causing queueing, skew in data distribution across slices, vacuum and analyze overhead after swap, and downstream consumer dependency on fresh data by 07:00 UTC. Row-count verification between source (manifest file) and target after every load. Tools available: AWS S3, AWS Redshift, AWS Glue, Airflow, dbt, Redshift Spectrum, manifest files.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['AWS S3', 'Redshift', 'AWS Glue', 'Airflow', 'dbt', 'Redshift Spectrum']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

response_content:
{
  "id": "db-07-s3-redshift-load-plan",
  "goal_id": "db-07-s3-redshift-load",
  "version": 1,
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "fetch_manifest",
      "description": "Fetch the manifest file from S3",
      "action": "fetch",
      "target": "s3://my-bucket/manifest.json",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "S3 bucket is accessible",
          "fact": "s3_accessible",
          "established_by": "env"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "load_to_staging",
      "description": "Load data from S3 to Redshift staging table",
      "action": "copy",
      "target": "redshift_staging_table",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "COPY command fails",
        "action": "empty staging table",
        "safety_guard": "ensure staging table is empty"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "row count in staging table",
        "how": "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM redshift_staging_table",
        "expected": "matches count in manifest file"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Manifest file is fetched",
          "fact": "manifest_fetched",
          "established_by": "fetch_manifest"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "data_validation",
      "description": "Validate data in the staging table",
      "action": "validate",
      "target": "redshift_staging_table",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "data validation fails",
        "action": "notify failure",
        "safety_guard": "log details of validation failure"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "data consistency",
        "how": "run validation checks",
        "expected": "data passes all validation checks"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Data is loaded to staging",
          "fact": "data_loaded",
          "established_by": "load_to_staging"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "swap_partitions",
      "description": "Swap the new partition with the current partition",
      "action": "swap",
      "target": "redshift_table",
      "risk_class": "critical",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "partition swap fails",
        "action": "rollback to previous partition",
        "safety_guard": "ensure previous partition is intact"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "row count in target table",
        "how": "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM redshift_table",
        "expected": "matches count in staging table"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Data validation is successful",
          "fact": "data_validated",
          "established_by": "data_validation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vacuum_analyze",
      "description": "Vacuum and analyze the target Redshift table",
      "action": "vacuum",
      "target": "redshift_table",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Partition swap is complete",
          "fact": "partition_swapped",
          "established_by": "swap_partitions"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from_task": "fetch_manifest",
      "to_task": "load_to_staging",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "load_to_staging",
      "to_task": "data_validation",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "data_validation",
      "to_task": "swap_partitions",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "swap_partitions",
      "to_task": "vacuum_analyze",
      "kind": "hard"
    }
  ],
  "branches": []
}
